intent: >
  Guarantee every homepage lead carries contact info by making email
  required at the HTML level, closing the no-JS gap left by the old
  client-side phone-or-email check.

slice: ?/?
kind: feature
behavior_change: breaking

reversibility: reversible

scope:
  declared:
    - src/index.njk
    - src/assets/js/application.js
    - src/assets/js/controllers/contact_form_controller.js
  actual:
    - src/index.njk
    - src/assets/js/application.js
    - src/assets/js/controllers/contact_form_controller.js
  drift: []

proof:
  tests_run: npm run build
  result: green
  failing: 0

tests:
  needed: "no"
  rationale: >
    Repo has no test infrastructure (static Eleventy site; scripts are
    dev/build/clean only). Proof is a clean build plus manual browser
    verification of the required-field behavior.

lint:
  run: none
  result: skipped
  count: 0
  rationale: >
    No linter configured in this repo.

verification:
  manual:
    - "npm run build compiles clean, no stale contact-form references (grep)"
    - "Browser check of required email planned in Chrome before push"

assumptions:
  - "no active plan — ad-hoc work; declared = files agreed in conversation"
  - "Browser-native constraint validation (required + type=email) is a sufficient floor; Web3Forms does no server-side field validation"
  - "Phone-only leads lost to the email requirement are acceptable — Tommy chose the guaranteed-email floor over the either/or UX"

specifications:
  - "Lead-capture floor: every lead form requires email via HTML required; phone is optional on top"

deviations_from_plan: none

addresses: []

trade_offs: >
  Chose HTML required on email over keeping the JS either/or check.
  Cost is that phone-preferring visitors must now supply an email;
  benefit is enforcement that survives JS failure. Keeping both was
  rejected as dead code — the JS branch could never fire.

self_review:
  tests: "No test framework in repo; build + manual browser check is the existing verification pattern."
  consistency: "Matches the required-attr + asterisk-label convention on Name, City, Project Details; removes the one-off JS validation pattern rather than adding a second way."
  api: "Removed the contact-form Stimulus identifier; grep confirms zero remaining consumers."
  dead_code: "Controller file and registration deleted with the wiring — nothing orphaned left behind."
  error_paths: "Empty/invalid email now blocked by browser constraint validation in all browsers, including no-JS."

confidence: high
reviewer_attention:
  - src/index.njk:672-684
